{"command": "cd /testbed && sed -n '100,320p' specs/001-transactions/spec.md; echo ===WC===; wc -l specs/001-transactions/spec.md; echo ===CHECKLISTS===; ls -la specs/001-transactions/checklists/ 2>&1; echo ===SPECIFY===; ls .specify/ 2>/dev/null; cat .specify/init-options.json 2>/dev/null; cat .specify/feature.json 2>/dev/null", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": "   before and after batch operations, **Then** all reads/writes behave exactly\n   as without the wrapper.\n2. **Given** a successful batch insert of a nested document, **When** the\n   caller mutates the original input document afterwards, **Then** the stored\n   document is unchanged; the returned inserted IDs identify the stored\n   documents.\n\n---\n\n### Edge Cases\n\n- Empty operations list: returns [] and leaves the table unchanged.\n- Remove targeting a missing document ID: an error; the whole batch rolls back.\n- doc_id that is 0, negative, or not an integer: ValueError (malformed).\n- Operation that is not a dictionary, or a list that is not a list of\n  dictionaries: ValueError.\n- Insert whose 'document' value is not a dict: ValueError.\n- A remove that targets a document inserted earlier in the same batch: allowed\n  (sequential application; the document exists at that point).\n- Failure after several successful operations: complete rollback of the\n  pre-batch state, including undoing earlier inserts and restores of earlier\n  removes within the same batch.\n- Nested documents (dicts and lists at any depth) in inserts: stored and\n  returned as copies, not aliases of the caller's input.\n\n## Requirements *(mandatory)*\n\n### Functional Requirements\n\n- **FR-001** (R01): BatchWriter MUST wrap a supplied TinyDB instance and expose\n  apply(operations), which accepts a list of operation dictionaries.\n- **FR-002** (R01): Each operation MUST be either {'op': 'insert',\n  'document': dict} or {'op': 'remove', 'doc_id': positive integer}; no other\n  operation kinds are supported; only the default table is used.\n- **FR-003** (R01): apply() MUST return the list of inserted document IDs in\n  insertion order; remove operations MUST add no result; empty input MUST\n  return [].\n- **FR-004** (R01): Unknown or malformed operations MUST raise ValueError\n  (including: op not 'insert'/'remove', missing or wrong-typed required fields,\n  doc_id not a positive integer, document not a dict, non-dict operation,\n  non-list input).\n- **FR-005** (R02): Batch application MUST be atomic: operations are validated\n  and applied sequentially, but on any error the complete pre-batch default-\n  table data MUST be restored and no partial changes may remain.\n- **FR-006** (R02): A remove targeting a missing document ID MUST be an error\n  and MUST trigger the rollback in FR-005.\n- **FR-007** (R02): Previously acquired handles to the default table (the table\n  obtained via db.table('_default') before the batch) MUST reflect both\n  successful application and rollback.\n- **FR-008** (R03): Ordinary TinyDB reads/writes and preexisting documents MUST\n  continue to work when a BatchWriter wraps the instance; the wrapper MUST NOT\n  change ordinary TinyDB behavior.\n- **FR-009** (R03): Inserted and returned nested data MUST NOT alias the\n  caller's input; mutating an operation (or its document) after apply() MUST\n  NOT mutate the database.\n\n### Key Entities\n\n- **TinyDB instance**: The supplied database that BatchWriter wraps; source of\n  the default table and of ordinary reads/writes. Not modified in its API.\n- **Default table**: The single table BatchWriter operates on; holds preexisting\n  and inserted documents; its complete data defines the pre-batch state for\n  rollback.\n- **Operation**: A dictionary describing one atomic step: an insert carrying a\n  document dict, or a remove carrying a positive integer document ID.\n- **Document**: A dict (possibly nested with lists/dicts) inserted into the\n  default table; stored as an independent copy of the caller's input.\n- **Document ID**: A positive integer identifying a document in the default\n  table; the unit of the return value of apply() and of remove targeting.\n\n## Success Criteria *(mandatory)*\n\n### Measurable Outcomes\n\n- **SC-001**: 100% of valid mixed insert/remove batches apply completely to the\n  default table and return exactly the inserted document IDs in insertion order\n  (removes contribute nothing).\n- **SC-002**: 100% of failing batches (missing-ID remove, malformed operation,\n  or error mid-batch) leave the default table byte-for-byte equal to its\n  pre-batch state, as observed through both the wrapper and previously acquired\n  table handles.\n- **SC-003**: 100% of unknown/malformed operations raise ValueError; empty\n  input returns [] in 100% of cases.\n- **SC-004**: 100% of ordinary TinyDB reads/writes and preexisting-document\n  accesses behave identically with and without the wrapper (no regressions in\n  the existing test suite).\n- **SC-005**: 0 aliasing faults: mutating caller input or returned data after\n  apply() never changes stored documents, for nested data at any depth.\n\n## Assumptions\n\n- **A1** (from R01): A 'positive integer' doc_id means an integer > 0; 0,\n  negatives, booleans, and non-integer values are malformed and raise\n  ValueError.\n- **A2** (from R02): \"Any error\" in atomicity includes malformed operations\n  (ValueError) and missing-ID removes; the raised error type for a missing-ID\n  remove is unspecified by the milestone and is left to the plan (it MUST\n  trigger rollback either way).\n- **A3** (from R02): \"Complete pre-batch default-table data\" is the exact set of\n  documents (with their IDs) present in the default table immediately before\n  apply() is called; rollback restores that exact state.\n- **A4** (from R03): \"Returned nested data\" refers to the returned list of\n  inserted document IDs plus the stored documents being independent copies of\n  the caller's input documents; apply() itself returns only IDs.\n- **A5** (scope): BatchWriter operates on the default table only; other tables\n  are out of scope and are not part of the batch/rollback contract.\n- **A6** (scope): The implementation lives in tinydb/journal.py; public\n  acceptance is acceptance_public.py; upstream tests remain unchanged; own\n  tests may be added.\n- **A7** (assumption): apply() is synchronous and single-threaded; concurrent\n  batch usage is out of scope for this milestone.\n===WC===\n210 specs/001-transactions/spec.md\n===CHECKLISTS===\ntotal 12\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 bench bench 4096 Oct 17 17:25 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 bench bench 4096 Oct 17 17:39 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 bench bench 2051 Oct 17 17:25 requirements.md\n===SPECIFY===\nfeature.json\nmemory\nscripts\ntemplates\n{\n  \"feature_directory\": \"specs/001-transactions\"\n}\n"}